module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.ChartBaseSection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesDegreeOneComparison

/-!
# Two charts of one `Proj` give the same comparison of `𝒪(1)` with an ideal

On `Proj 𝒮` for a nonnegatively graded ring `𝒮`, a degree-one element `f` trivializes the
twisting sheaf `𝒪(1)` over the standard open `D₊(f)`: a section `t` of `𝒪(1)` there is `f` times
a unique function, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.twistOneCoeff`. The comparison of
`𝒪(1)` with an ideal generated by a section `u` of the structure sheaf is "divide by `f`, then
multiply by `u`", and for the comparison to be independent of the chart the products
`twistOneCoeff f t · u` over two charts have to agree.

This file isolates the exact hypothesis that makes them agree —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.twistOneCoeff_mul_comm` — and supplies it for the
charts of a blowup of an *arbitrary* scheme, where the generator is the pullback of a section of
the base along the blowup morphism and the two descriptions of that pullback are identified by
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.chartBaseSection_val`.

The grading matters. The charts of `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp ℐ` are the `Proj` of
`(AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U`, not of
`Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading (ℐ.ideal U)`, so the statement proved here is at the former: it is the
general-base counterpart of `Stacks.Blowup.chartCoeff_mul_baseSectionRes_comm`, which is at the
latter and therefore only ever applies to a blowup of an affine scheme.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.twistOneCoeff`: a section of `𝒪(1)` over an open
  of `D₊(f)`, divided by the trivializing section of `f`. This is
  `Stacks.Blowup.chartCoeff` with the Rees algebra of a ring replaced by an arbitrary grading.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.algebraMap_mul_trivializingFun_comm`: a cross
  identity `z · g = w · f` between degree-one elements and ring elements becomes, at every point
  of `D₊(f) ∩ D₊(g)`, the identity `z · g⁻ᵛᵃˡ = w · f⁻ᵛᵃˡ` between constant fractions times
  trivializing values.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.twistOneCoeff_mul_comm`: **two charts of one
  `Proj` give the same comparison**, given that cross identity on the two generators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.twistOneCoeff_mul_chartBaseSectionRes_comm`: **the instance for a blowup of
  an arbitrary scheme.** Over an open of the chart over `U` contained in both `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` and
  `D₊(a'⁽¹⁾)` for two sections `a, a'` of the centre on `U`, dividing by `a⁽¹⁾` and multiplying by
  the pullback of `a` gives the same thing as dividing by `a'⁽¹⁾` and multiplying by the pullback
  of `a'`.

## Implementation notes

`twistOneCoeff` exists as a `def` with its target type written out as `Γ(Proj 𝒮, W)` rather than
as the domain of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization.trivializingEquiv`, which is
`(AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.structureSheaf 𝒮).obj.obj (op W)`. The two are
definitionally but not *reducibly* equal, so at the second spelling `HMul` synthesis fails and the
product that the whole file is about cannot be written down; a type ascription does not help,
because it does not change what `inferType` returns. Naming the spelling in a `def`'s stated type
does.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite HomogeneousLocalization
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (moduleSections twistGrading)

universe u w

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local instance] ProjectiveSpectrum.isPrime

variable {S : Type u} [CommRing S] {σ : Type w} [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

/-- **The chartwise trivializing coefficient of `𝒪(1)`**: a section of `𝒪(1)` over an open
contained in `D₊(f)`, for `f` of degree one, divided by the trivializing section of `f`. -/
def twistOneCoeff {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
    (t : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) W) :
    Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮, W) :=
  (trivializingEquiv 𝒮 hf 1 hW).symm t

/-- **The trivializing coefficient inverts multiplication by the trivializing section.** -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_val_mul {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
    (t : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) W) (x : W) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val ((twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW t).1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hW x
      = t.1 x :=
  val_trivializingEquiv_symm_mul 𝒮 hf 1 hW t x

/-- The trivializing coefficient is additive. -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_add {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
    (t t' : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) W) :
    twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW (t + t') = twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW t + twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW t' :=
  map_add (trivializingEquiv 𝒮 hf 1 hW).symm t t'

/-- **The trivializing coefficient is linear over the functions on `D₊(f)`.** The scalar is
written at the spelling the twist sections carry, since at the spelling `Γ(Proj 𝒮, W)` the
`HSMul` instance is not found. -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_smul {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
    (r : ToType ((AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.structureSheaf 𝒮).obj.obj (op W)))
    (t : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) W) :
    twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW (r • t)
      = (show Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮, W) from r) * twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW t :=
  map_smul (trivializingEquiv 𝒮 hf 1 hW).symm r t

/-- **The trivializing coefficient commutes with restriction.** Pointwise both sides are the
value of `t` divided by the trivializing value, which is given by one formula. -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_map {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) {V W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hV : V ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f)
    (hWV : W ≤ V) (t : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) V) :
    twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hW
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf 𝒮 1).val.restrictₛₗ
          (homOfLE hWV).op t)
      = (((AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op)).hom
          (twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hV t) :=
  Subtype.ext (funext fun x => eq_of_val_mul_eq 𝒮 1 hW x
    ((twistOneCoeff_val_mul 𝒮 hf hW _ x).trans
      (twistOneCoeff_val_mul 𝒮 hf hV t ⟨x.1, hWV x.2⟩).symm))

/-- **A cross identity between two degree-one elements becomes an identity of constant fractions
times trivializing values.** If `z · g = w · f` in `𝒮`, then at every point of
`D₊(f) ∩ D₊(g)` the constant fraction of `z` times the trivializing value of `g` is the constant
fraction of `w` times the trivializing value of `f`. -/
theorem algebraMap_mul_trivializingFun_comm {f g : S} {z w : S}
    {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hWf : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) (hWg : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 g)
    (hzw : z * g = w * f) (x : W) :
    algebraMap S (Localization x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl) z *
        trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWg x
      = algebraMap S (Localization x.1.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.primeCompl) w *
        trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWf x := by
  rw [trivializingFun, trivializingFun, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap,
    ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, Localization.mk_mul, Localization.mk_mul]
  refine Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff.mpr (Localization.r_of_eq ?_)
  simp only [Int.toNat_one, pow_one, show ((-1 : ℤ)).toNat = 0 from rfl, pow_zero, one_mul]
  rw [hzw]

/-- **Two charts of one `Proj` give the same comparison of `𝒪(1)` with an ideal.** Dividing a
section of `𝒪(1)` by the trivializing section of `f` and multiplying by `u` gives the same thing
as dividing by that of `g` and multiplying by `v`, as soon as `u` and `v` satisfy the cross
identity against the two trivializing values. -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_mul_comm {f g : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) (hg : g ∈ 𝒮 1)
    {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮)}
    (hWf : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 f) (hWg : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒮 g)
    (u v : Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮, W))
    (huv : ∀ x : W, HomogeneousLocalization.val (u.1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWg x
      = HomogeneousLocalization.val (v.1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWf x)
    (t : moduleSections 𝒮 (twistGrading 𝒮 1) W) :
    twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hWf t * u = twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hg hWg t * v := by
  refine Subtype.ext (funext fun x => HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective _ ?_)
  have hA := twistOneCoeff_val_mul 𝒮 hf hWf t x
  have hB := twistOneCoeff_val_mul 𝒮 hg hWg t x
  show HomogeneousLocalization.val ((twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hf hWf t).1 x * u.1 x)
      = HomogeneousLocalization.val ((twistOneCoeff 𝒮 hg hWg t).1 x * v.1 x)
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul]
  refine ((isUnit_trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWf x).mul
    (isUnit_trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWg x)).mul_right_cancel ?_
  linear_combination
    (HomogeneousLocalization.val (u.1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWg x) * hA -
      (HomogeneousLocalization.val (v.1 x) * trivializingFun 𝒮 1 hWf x) * hB + t.1 x * (huv x)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTrivialization
open Stacks.RelativeProj

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local instance] ProjectiveSpectrum.isPrime

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (ℐ : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens)

/-- **The two chartwise comparisons of `𝒪(1)` with the exceptional ideal inside one chart of the
blowup of an arbitrary scheme agree.** Over an open of `Proj 𝒜(U)` contained in the standard
opens of the degree-one generators of two sections `a, a'` of the centre on `U`, dividing by
`a⁽¹⁾` and multiplying by the pullback of `a` gives the same thing as dividing by `a'⁽¹⁾` and
multiplying by the pullback of `a'`.

The cross identity is `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionRingBaseMap_mul_reesDegreeOne_comm` and the two
pullbacks are read as constant fractions by
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.chartBaseSection_val`. -/
theorem twistOneCoeff_mul_chartBaseSectionRes_comm (a a' : ℐ.ideal U)
    {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1))}
    (hWa : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1)
      (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a).1)
    (hWa' : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1)
      (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a').1)
    (t : moduleSections ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1)
      (twistGrading ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1) 1) W) :
    twistOneCoeff ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1) (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a).2 hWa t *
        (reesSituation ℐ).chartBaseSectionRes U.1 U.2 (a : Γ(X, U.1)) W
      = twistOneCoeff ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1) (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a').2 hWa' t *
        (reesSituation ℐ).chartBaseSectionRes U.1 U.2 (a' : Γ(X, U.1)) W := by
  refine twistOneCoeff_mul_comm _ (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a).2 (reesDegreeOne ℐ U a').2 hWa hWa'
    _ _ (fun x => ?_) t
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun y => y * trivializingFun ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1) 1 hWa' x)
    ((reesSituation ℐ).chartBaseSectionRes_val_eq U.1 U.2 (a : Γ(X, U.1)) x)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg
    (fun y => y * trivializingFun ((reesSituation ℐ).sectionRingGrading U.1) 1 hWa x)
    ((reesSituation ℐ).chartBaseSectionRes_val_eq U.1 U.2 (a' : Γ(X, U.1)) x)).symm
  exact algebraMap_mul_trivializingFun_comm _ hWa hWa'
    (sectionRingBaseMap_mul_reesDegreeOne_comm ℐ U (a : Γ(X, U.1)) (a' : Γ(X, U.1)) a a' rfl rfl)
    x

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
